---
// The c.ai migration page — the churn-intent twin of import-character-cards.
// That page answers "how do I import a card"; this one answers "Character.AI
// is winding down, where do I go". Every claim comes from the real code
// paths (charcard.ts, chathist.ts, chat-import-job.ts — incl.
// IMPORT_WELCOME_BONUS_TOKENS) so keep the copy honest when those move.
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";
import { LINKS, SITE_ORIGIN } from "../../lib/config";

export const prerender = true;
const discordStart = "/account?start=discord&next=" + encodeURIComponent("/dashboard?welcome=1#import");

// Steps mirror the visible "Get them out" list — the markup must describe
// the same content or it's structured-data spam.
const howTo = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "HowTo",
  name: "How to move a character from Character.AI to Discord",
  description: "Export a character card and chat history from Character.AI with CAI Tools, then import them as a private companion on Characterly — history included, so they remember you.",
  step: [
    { "@type": "HowToStep", position: 1, name: "Export with CAI Tools", text: "Open your chat on Character.AI with the CAI Tools browser extension and download the character card plus a Tavern-format .jsonl chat export.", url: `${SITE_ORIGIN}/guides/leaving-character-ai` },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", position: 2, name: "Continue with Discord", text: "Sign in with your Discord account. It links your Characterly account automatically.", url: `${SITE_ORIGIN}/account` },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", position: 3, name: "Drop in your files", text: "Drop the card and the chat export into the import section on your dashboard. The persona comes across; the history distills into real, private memories.", url: `${SITE_ORIGIN}/dashboard#import` },
  ],
};
---
<Base
  title="Leaving Character.AI? Bring your character with you · Characterly"
  description="Character.AI has filed for bankruptcy and is up for sale. Export your character card and chat history, then import them as a private companion on Characterly — memory included, with a welcome bonus on your first import."
  path="/guides/leaving-character-ai"
  jsonLd={[howTo]}
>
  <article class="wrap guide">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/guides/import-character-cards">Guides</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Leaving Character.AI</span></nav>
    <header class="guide-head">
      <h1>Bring them <em>home</em>.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Character.AI has filed for bankruptcy and is up for sale — if no buyer keeps it running, the service winds down. If your companion lives there, two files are all it takes to bring them — and everything you built together — somewhere they can stay.</p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="g-out">
      <h2 id="g-out">Step one: get them out</h2>
      <p class="body">Character.AI doesn't offer a one-click export, so the community built one. The <strong>CAI Tools</strong> browser extension is the standard way:</p>
      <ol class="how">
        <li><span class="n">1</span><div><h3>Install CAI Tools</h3><p>Add it to a desktop browser (Chrome or a Chromium-based browser), then open Character.AI while you're still able to sign in.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="n">2</span><div><h3>Save the card</h3><p>Open your character (or one you made) and use CAI Tools' card download — you'll get a <code>.png</code> or <code>.json</code> character card. That file is the character: persona, greeting, example dialogue.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="n">3</span><div><h3>Save your history</h3><p>In the chat you want to keep, use <strong>"Download as Tavern chat"</strong> — a <code>.jsonl</code> transcript of the conversation. Do this for each chat you care about; once access goes, it goes.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="muted">One character card per character, one <code>.jsonl</code> per conversation. Keep the files somewhere safe — they're yours.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="g-in">
      <h2 id="g-in">Step two: bring them in</h2>
      <ol class="how">
        <li><span class="n">1</span><div><h3>Continue with Discord</h3><p>Sign in with your Discord account below — that's where your companion lives, in your DMs and any servers you choose.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="n">2</span><div><h3>Drop in the files</h3><p>The <a href="/dashboard#import">import section on your dashboard</a> takes the card file and the chat export. Persona, greeting and example dialogue come across — alternate greetings too, as openings you pick between at first meet, and the card's character book becomes world lore that surfaces when the conversation touches it. The history is distilled into the companion's journal — real memories it can actually use, not a transcript it can't read back. The file itself is discarded.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="n">3</span><div><h3>Say hello again</h3><p>Your first completed history import lands <strong>150 welcome tokens</strong> on your account — enough for the import itself and the days while you settle in. The companion is <strong>private to you</strong>; nothing is published unless you choose to put it on <a href="/characters">the shelf</a>.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="actions"><a class="btn btn-go" href={discordStart} data-beacon="discord_signin_click"><Icon name="discord" size={18} />Continue with Discord</a></p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="g-diff">
      <h2 id="g-diff">What's different here</h2>
      <dl class="facts">
        <div><dt>Where they live</dt><dd>In your Discord DMs — and in real servers you invite them to, alongside your friends, not a walled-off room.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Memory</dt><dd>Yours to see. <code>/memory list</code>, the dashboard memory panel, and <code>/memory export</code> show everything a companion keeps — pin it, edit it, or forget it.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Privacy</dt><dd>Imports stay private by default, the transcript file is deleted after distilling, and <code>/opt-out</code> wipes it all. The repo is open if you'd rather run it yourself.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Reply retries</dt><dd>Right-click a companion's reply → Apps → Regenerate, and it takes another pass — the swipe you already know, without leaving Discord.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Cost</dt><dd>Free every day (30 tokens, ~15 exchanges). Premium is $7.99/month. Or bring your own API key and pay nothing but the provider's bill.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="g-faq">
      <h2 id="g-faq">Quick answers</h2>
      <dl class="facts">
        <div><dt>My chat is huge</dt><dd>Imports take the first 4,000 turns — the foundation of the relationship — and resume where they left off if interrupted.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Group chats?</dt><dd>The speaker who isn't you and talks most becomes the companion, so two personas never blend into one.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Changed my mind</dt><dd>The dashboard and <code>/companion imports</code> list every import and undo any of them, memories and all.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Not on Discord?</dt><dd>Companions live there — that's the product. If Discord isn't for you, the <a href={LINKS.discord} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Characterly server</a> is the gentlest way to try it anyway.</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="actions"><a class="link" href="/guides/import-character-cards">The full import reference</a><a class="link" href="/characters">Browse the shelf</a></p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .guide > * { max-width: 880px; }
  .guide h1 { font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 72px); }
  .crumbs { display: flex; gap: 8px; padding-top: 28px; font-size: 14.5px; font-weight: 650; color: var(--ink-3); }
  .crumbs a { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .guide-head { padding: 28px 0 8px; }
  .guide-head .lede { margin-top: 20px; }
  .guide section { padding-top: 56px; }
  .guide h2 { font-size: clamp(26px, 2.6vw, 36px); margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .how { list-style: none; display: grid; gap: 0; border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); }
  .how li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 18px; padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .how .n { width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 50%; display: grid; place-items: center; background: var(--ink); color: #fff; font-weight: 850; }
  .how h3 { margin: 0; }
  .how p { margin-top: 4px; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 62ch; }
  .how a { font-weight: 700; }
  .facts { display: grid; border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); }
  .facts > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 180px 1fr; gap: 20px; padding: 14px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .facts dt { font-weight: 750; }
  .facts dd { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .guide section > .muted, .body { margin-top: 16px; max-width: 66ch; }
  .body { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 18px; }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 8px 24px; margin-top: 24px; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .facts > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; } }
</style>
